From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:57:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/25] UefiPayloadPkg: Import coreboot's TPM 2.0 event log

coreboot measures its own stages into the TPM and keeps a TCG TPM 2.0
event log in CBMEM. Tcg2Dxe starts a separate EFI event log, so without
coreboot's events the EFI log can't explain PCR 2, and coreboot's log
alone can't explain anything edk2 measured.

Find coreboot's log in CBMEM and turn each event into a
gTcgEvent2EntryHob, which Tcg2Dxe copies into the EFI log as it would
events from a PEI phase. Skip coreboot's Spec ID Event: Tcg2Dxe writes
its own, listing the active PCR banks.

Based on Dasharo's "DasharoPayloadPkg,SecurityPkg: import coreboot's
TPM log" (Sergii Dmytruk), which does this in BlSupportPei. The
UefiPayloadPkg has no PEI phase, so this runs in UefiPayloadEntry, and
it handles TPM 2.0 logs only.

Link: https://github.com/Dasharo/edk2/commit/27b3afc03924cc029d175269025a3af2921dee9c
Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
